    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 212332\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n332 PM PST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Minimal weather impacts through next week. \n\n* A weak disturbance will bring a few showers to northern areas \n  later Sunday through Monday, including a couple of inches of snow \n  over the Sierras.\n\n* Building ridge with steady warming Tuesday through next weekend, \n  pushing above normal by Thanksgiving. Saturday could be well above \n  normal. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...\nWeak high pressure aloft will maintain cool and calm conditions \nthrough Sunday morning. A short-wave trough will move through the \nregion later Sunday through Monday. High chances for light rain and \nsnow over the Sierra. Elevations above 4,500 feet should see a few \ninches of snow, with a dusting down to 3,500 feet. While the chances \nare low, cannot discount a light shower or two anywhere north of Las \nVegas. Southwest winds will also increase over the mountains and \nwestern Mojave with gusts of 25 to 35 mph common. Wind advisories\nare unlikely. High pressure aloft will steadily build after and \ntemperatures will rise as a result. Expecting warming each day \nTuesday through Saturday, going above normal by Thanksgiving. \nTemperatures could push 10 degrees above normal by Saturday. \nLooking for a pattern change the following week with multiple \nchances of rain and gusty winds. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Winds\nwill remain light and somewhat variable through the forecast \nperiod, but will generally follow daily directional patterns. \nAfter sunset, winds will shift to the west, with another round of \nlight southeasterly winds expected Sunday afternoon. Increasing \nmid-level and high clouds are expected this evening onward, with \nbases at or above 15kft. VFR conditions prevail.\n\n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast\nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Elevated northerly\nwinds along the Lower Colorado River Valley in the vicinity of \nKIFP will become light and variable this evening. Elsewhere, winds\nremain light through the forecast period, and generally follow \ntypical daily directional patterns with some variability. Mid-\nlevel and high clouds will continue expanding across the region \nfrom west to east through tonight, though bases are expected to \nremain at or above 15kft. VFR conditions prevail.\n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Kittell\nAVIATION...Phillipson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
